  message: "Cross-item review 2026-05-17: investigation found the original kill-the-field framing was wrong. docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:263 declares this field with a 🟪 status marker (per the spec's legend at line 14, 🟪 = 'needs design — requires more design thinking before implementation'). Spec line 781 describes the designed sub-shape: 'quality.reason remains for human debugging but is NOT relied upon for programmatic logic.' So the designed shape is quality={'score': ..., 'reason': '...'}. 100% null in current output is the CORRECT state for a 🟪 field with no producer yet — killing the field would erase a designed placeholder and create new spec-vs-data drift. Description rewritten to reframe as a design call: either advance 🟪 design to ⬜/🟨 with a concrete QualityScore definition and at least one producer, OR retire QualityScore from the spec AND the field together. The honest framing is 'design decision needed,' not 'dead field to delete.'"  # 48ea
